rmaceutical company, focuses on the discovery and development of precision peptide therapies for the treatment of endocrine and metabolic disorders. Its lead product candidate is Canvuparatide (MBX 2109), a parathyroid hormone peptide prodrug, which is in Phase 3 clinical trial for the treatment of chronic hypoparathyroidism. The company is also developing Imapextide (MBX 1416), a long-acting glucagon-like peptide-1 (GLP-1) receptor antagonist that is in Phase 2 clinical trial a potential therapy for post-bariatric hypoglycemia, a chronic complication of bariatric surgery. In addition, it is developing MBX 4291, a lead obesity product candidate, which is in investigational new drug-enabling studies for the treatment of obesity and co-morbidities. The company was founded in 2018 and is based in Carmel, Indiana.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Steven L. Hoerter | Executive Chairperson, CEO & President | Age 54 | Compensation: $40,477 (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 63 people. Stock-based compensation of $138K per employee reflects an ownership culture. Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (8/10).","financial_summary":["MBX Biosciences, Inc. is a mid-cap healthcare business with a $2.8B market cap.","The company is burning through $82M of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","On the balance sheet, interest coverage of 40\u00d7 is fortress-like.","Net dilution runs at 21.7% annually, transferring value from owners to stock-based comp, and insiders hold 2.8% of the shares."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Piotroski score 3/9 \u2014 the fundamentals are deteriorating on multiple fronts","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Elevated short interest (11.9% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting the other way","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (88% sell ratio, net $2.5M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev"